        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Re: the `buffer-open` section:\r\n\r\n- Running `bufload()` as described will cause any setlocal window options within `ftplugin` scripts to do nothing (such as setting per-filetype listchars or wrap). I think this is because `f_bufload` calls `buf_ensure_loaded` which then calls `aucmd_prepbuf` to put the buffer in a temporary window. But this problem existed before the recent PRs addressing that function.\r\n\r\n- Not directly mentioned but related - Using `help` to open a help window calls `prepare_help_buffer` within `do_ecmd`, which sets the `help-buffer-options` using `w_onebuf_opt` before firing `FileType`. I'm not sure how to re-create this programmatically without disabling `FileType` to pre-set locals.",
            "created_at": "2026-06-24T06:34:04Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40378#issuecomment-4786532092",
            "id": 4786532092,
            "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/40378",
            "minimized": null,
