        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "`bufadd` > `:buffer` seems to work. It calls `do_buffer_ext` like `nvim_set_current_buf` does (and I've never had an issue with `nvim_set_current_buf` as long as `bufload` isn't run manually beforehand).\r\n\r\nShouldn't even need `:edit` afterwards.\r\n\r\nEDIT: Or maybe not. If I just do `:buffer`, when my autocmd to go to the `\"` runs, it always shows as `{ 1, 0 }`. Whereas if I use `:edit` it works.",
